{title: At Calvary (I Am Free)}
{artist: William Reed Newell, Daniel Brink Towner, C. Michael Pilato}
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 98}

Verse 1
[Bm]Years I spent in vanity and pride,
[F]Caring not my Lord was [Bm]crucified,
[Gm]Knowing not it was for [Emadd2]me He died on [Fsus]Calvary.

Verse 2
[Bm]By God's Word at last my sin I learned,
[F]Then I trembled at the law I'd [Bm]spurned,
[Gm]Till my guilty soul [Emadd2]imploring turned to [Fsus]Calvary.

Chorus
[Em]Mercy there was great and [Bm]grace was free.
[F]Pardon there was multiplied [Bm]to [Bm/D]me.
[Em]There my burdened soul found [Bm]liberty at [Fsus]Calvary!

Verse 3
[Bm]Oh the love that drew salvation's plan!
[F]Oh the grace that brought it [Bm]down to man!
[Gm]Oh the mighty gulf that [Emadd2]God did span at [Fsus]Calvary!

Chorus
[Em]Mercy there was great and [Bm]grace was free.
[F]Pardon there was multiplied [Bm]to [Bm/D]me.
[Em]There my burdened soul found [Bm]liberty at [Fsus]Calvary!

Verse 4
[Bm]I am free.  [Emmaj7]I am free.
[Bm/D]By the mercy [Cm7]of God's [Bm/D]great grace, [Em]I am free.
[F]I am free ([Emmaj7]and I am forgiven).  I am free ([Bm/D]and now I am living).
By the mercy [Cm7]of God's [Bm/D]great grace, [Em]I am free.

Verse 5
[Bm]Now I give to Jesus everything.
[F]Now I gladly own Him [Bm]as my King.
[Gm]Now my raptured soul can [Emadd2]only sing of [Fsus]Calvary!
